<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PermissionSetGroup xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <description>Junior Acquisitions Analyst: Edit on Acquisition + Disposition + Contact (brokers), View-only on Transaction + Property Management + Task checklist fields, plus Acquisition/Disposition/Transaction app+tab visibility (no PM app).</description>
    <label>DPEG Junior Analyst PSG</label>
    <!--
        Opportunity_Stage_Actions_Access joined this group on 2026-08-10 and THIS GROUP ONLY.
        It is the layer-4 CAPABILITY set for the Opportunity and child-object stage quick
        actions; the Junior Analyst is the only deal-driver persona. The other three groups are
        deliberately excluded: DPEG_Principal_PSG approves rather than drives and is read-only on
        Opportunity by design; DPEG_Transaction_Team holds Opportunity read-only; and
        DPEG_Property_Management_Team is out of module.

        ⚠ ORDER MATTERS AND THE ORDER IS NOT OBVIOUS. On the day it was added this membership
        granted ZERO additional effective access, because the same four Apex classes were still
        in DPEG_Apex_Access, which is also in this group - permission sets union. The membership
        only becomes load-bearing once StageAdvanceController and OpportunityApprovalController
        are removed from that catch-all. So: DEPLOY AND JOIN FIRST -> WAIT FOR GROUP
        RECALCULATION (status must read Updated) -> VERIFY AS A REAL DEAL DRIVER -> ONLY THEN
        TRIM DPEG_Apex_Access. Reversing those two deploys breaks every deal-driver stage button
        in the window between them.

        ⚠ THIS MEMBERSHIP IS NOT THE WHOLE GATE. Driving a stage also requires factor (a),
        Acquisition_Deal_Driver's FLS read on User.Deal_Driver__c, AND factor (b),
        Deal_Driver__c = true on the driver's own User record. Acquisition_Deal_Driver is
        assigned DIRECTLY rather than through this group on purpose: adding it here would hand
        factor (a) to the group's ENTIRE population in one move, collapsing the gate to the
        single remaining factor for everyone in it. Note that (b) is a field VALUE on a User
        record - no permission set can grant it, which is exactly why the two factors are
        independent and why only (a) is at risk from a membership change.

        SharePoint_Integration_Access joined this group on 2026-08-11 (SharePoint deal-folder
        feature, design D1-A/scoped-persona user decision) and THIS GROUP ONLY. The user
        deliberately declined DPEG_Transaction_Team even though the design doc's default
        recommendation lists both persona groups - do not "correct" this by adding it there.
        Membership was reconciled against the org before this edit; the deployed group carried no
        member absent from this file (see ARCHITECTURE.md §2's 2026-08-10 finding on this exact
        hazard - a PermissionSetGroup deploy replaces its member list wholesale).
    -->
    <permissionSets>DPEG_Acquisition_Edit</permissionSets>
    <permissionSets>DPEG_Apex_Access</permissionSets>
    <permissionSets>DPEG_App_Acquisition</permissionSets>
    <permissionSets>DPEG_App_Disposition</permissionSets>
    <permissionSets>DPEG_App_Transaction</permissionSets>
    <permissionSets>DPEG_Base_Access</permissionSets>
    <permissionSets>DPEG_Contact_Edit</permissionSets>
    <permissionSets>DPEG_Disposition_Edit</permissionSets>
    <permissionSets>DPEG_PropertyMgmt_View</permissionSets>
    <permissionSets>DPEG_TaskChecklist_View</permissionSets>
    <permissionSets>DPEG_Transaction_View</permissionSets>
    <permissionSets>Opportunity_Stage_Actions_Access</permissionSets>
    <permissionSets>SharePoint_Integration_Access</permissionSets>
</PermissionSetGroup>
